In the conventional Standard Model normalization, $\begin{aligned}
  H(x)&=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \begin{pmatrix}
    0\\ v+h(x)
  \end{pmatrix},
  \\
  m_f&=\frac{y_fv}{\sqrt2},
  \\
  \mathcal L_{hff}&=-\frac{m_f}{v}h\bar f f,
\end{aligned}$ with $v\simeq246\,\mathrm{GeV}$. The lecture’s rough $F\sim200\,\mathrm{GeV}$ is this same electroweak scale with normalization details suppressed.

